<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  Creature stat-block errors (D110): a mount's _Monster text is parsed at
  pack build into _Creature Stat Block, so a garbled line becomes a
  mount.stat-block-unparsed diagnostic and a wrong card. Merged after the
  CBLoader parts by scripts/build-private-content.sh. The owner allows the
  corrected official block text here (as 9F-associates.part restores
  associate text from the compendium).

  Summoned creatures (D111) are parsed the same way from a summon power's
  stat fields; a garbled damage line prints as text and is a
  summon.stat-block-unparsed diagnostic.
-->
<D20Rules game-system="D&amp;D4E">
  <!-- Cat (Dragon 399, CBLoader 40-gear.part): the block carries a stray
       "Large natural beast (mount) - XP 175" line above its real "Tiny
       natural beast - XP 25" line, and the typo "Skills s Athletics". The
       record's own Full Text has the right block; restore it. -->
  <RemoveNodes internal-id="ID_D399_GEAR_CAT"><specific name="_Monster" /></RemoveNodes>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_D399_GEAR_CAT">
    <specific name="_Monster">Cat - Level 1 Minion Skirmisher
Tiny  natural beast - XP 25
Initiative +6 Senses Perception +1; low-light vision
HP 1; a missed attack never damages a minion.
AC 15; Fortitude 10, Reflex 14, Will 11
Speed 7

Cat’s Stealth (Move Action; at-will)
While within 10 squares of the cat, the cat’s master can move up to half his or her speed without incurring the –5 penalty to Stealth checks for moving more than 2 squares.

Skills Athletics +2, Stealth +9
Str 4 (-3) ◦ Dex 19 (+4) ◦ Wis 12 (+1)
Con 11 (+0) ◦ Int 2 (-4) ◦ Cha 11 (0)
Alignment Unaligned Languages -</specific>
  </AppendNodes>

  <!-- Bound Soul (Dragon 427, CBLoader 38-paragon-paths.part): both damage
       lines of its Standard Action read "your intelligence, Wisdom, or
       Charisma necrotic and radiant damage", dropping "modifier". Restore
       the word (the owner allows this much official text) so the line
       parses as the highest of the three modifiers, as native
       MultipleAbilityChoices reads "X, Y, or Z modifier". The Minor and
       Opportunity Action fields are re-added unchanged after it, so the
       actions keep their order. -->
  <RemoveNodes internal-id="ID_DRAG427_SOUL">
    <specific name="Standard Action" />
    <specific name="Minor Action" />
    <specific name="Opportunity Action" />
  </RemoveNodes>
  <AppendNodes internal-id="ID_DRAG427_SOUL">
    <specific name="Standard Action"> (At-Will)
Attack: Melee 1 (one creature); your level + 5 vs. Fortitude
Hit: 1d10 + your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier necrotic and radiant damage.
Level 21: 2d10 + your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier necrotic and radiant damage.</specific>
    <specific name="Minor Action"> (At-Will)
Effect: The soul walks, shifts, runs, stands up, squeezes, or crawls. </specific>
    <specific name="Opportunity Action"> (At-Will)
Trigger: An enemy hits you with a melee attack while you are adjacent to the soul.
Effect: The soul can push the triggering enemy 1 square.
Level 21: The soul pushes the triggering enemy up to 3 squares. </specific>
  </AppendNodes>
</D20Rules>
